  "narrative": "Supported findings. The strongest dataset-only association is feature_010=1 versus 0: the marginal claim H8 remains accepted with signed estimate 0.829 (0.767 to 0.891), and the newly delivered independent validation for H15 strengthens the same signal within the feature_003=0 stratum: signed estimate 0.760 (0.664 to 0.856), with R16 previously showing 0.841 (0.774 to 0.909). Together with accepted within-stratum contrasts in high feature_040, feature_018, feature_036, and feature_038 cells, this establishes a robust threshold-sized feature_010 association in this supplied dataset, not causality or generalizability.\n\nThe second strong supported finding is feature_037, but in the direction opposite to the original broad screen. H43 is explicitly reassessed and rejected because its validation R39 gives signed -0.811 (-0.904 to -0.717), confirming the large negative raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast already seen in R37 (-0.804, -0.867 to -0.742). The scientifically meaningful claim is therefore the reversed claim H45: feature_037=1 versus 0 is associated with a lower composite dependency score by about 0.80-0.81 units, meaning stronger dependency. This claim has both discovery R37 and independent validation R39, so I accept it as active while its relationship to feature_010 is tested.\n\nNegative or non-threshold findings. H5 is reassessed using its independent validation response. Both R5 and R13 are positive and exclude the null (signed estimates 0.139 and 0.145), but their point estimates are below the 0.15-unit threshold and their intervals remain compatible with effects below threshold. I keep H5 unresolved and deferred as a possible subthreshold or borderline feature_003 association, not as an accepted meaningful effect. The feature_003 subgroup line is otherwise closed: H25 validation failed to confirm its discovery estimate, H37 failed to demonstrate clear upper-quartile specificity, H26 was null or weak, and H14 remains imprecise and is now closed as unresolved. The binary screens for feature_007, feature_058, feature_015, feature_041, feature_047, feature_048, feature_001, feature_011, feature_006, feature_031, feature_023, and related feature_010 interactions are negative or too small to support threshold-sized claims.\n\nMost informative next analyses are the feature_037 versus feature_010 disentanglement checks. The registered H46 and H47 test feature_037 within feature_010=0 and feature_010=1, while H48 tests feature_037 effect modification by feature_010. I also register new H50-H52-style claims to test feature_010 within feature_037=0 and feature_010=1 and a feature_010-by-feature_037 interaction. These comparisons will reveal whether feature_037 and feature_010 represent partially redundant measured proxies or separate strong associations in this dataset.",
  "research_notes": "Dataset-only synthesis. Accepted robust associations: feature_010=1 vs 0 (H8, with stratum confirmations H15/H16/H27/H32-H34; H15 now independently validated by R40) and reversed feature_037=1 vs 0 (H45 accepted from R37 and validation R39; raw negative means more negative outcome/stronger dependency). H43 is rejected/closed because it was a direction-misaligned broad screen, not because feature_037 lacks association. Feature_003 remains marginal: H5 unresolved/deferred after validation (R5/R13 positive but below threshold), H13 deferred, H14 unresolved/closed, H25/H37 upper-log_pfs lead closed as not threshold-specific, H26 rejected, H29-H31 closed. Broad screens mostly null: feature_007/058/015/041/047/048/001/011/006/031/023. Feature_010 interactions with feature_003/feature_040/feature_038 are not meaningful. Next priority: disentangle feature_037 and feature_010 via H46-H48 plus new feature_010-within-feature_037 stratum tests and interaction. If one attenuates strongly in the other's strata, interpret as redundant/proxy association in this dataset; if both persist, they are separate measured associations. No causal or generalizable claim yet."
